O .claude/skills/security-scan/references/scan-layers.md 71-71 PL R116 SEC-003 | Untrusted payloads must not deserialize into arbitrary runtime types. | Suspected EXTRA security invariant inside investigation prompts. Kept oracle-linked: SEC-003 treats data crossing the trust boundary as untrusted; type-driven deserialization of untrusted payloads is the canonical violation of that trust assumption. | Polymorphic deserialization of untrusted input is flagged and must be avoided.
O CLAUDE.md 38-39 PL R290,R291 ARC-020 | adding a major library or framework | Suspected EXTRA approval gates (major libraries; project-wide conventions). Kept oracle-linked: ARC-020's list is open ('consequential choices such as ...') and already includes a project-wide Result model and replacement of approved technology; a major framework or a project-wide convention is the same class of consequential choice. The broader dependency gate of the five-question test is registered separately as X48. | Adding e.g. a major UI or ORM framework needs approval.
O .editorconfig 7-66 PL R332 RUN-009,RUN-024 | csharp_style_namespace_declarations = file_scoped:suggestion | Considered whether concrete .editorconfig values (indentation, var, naming) are EXTRA. Kept oracle-linked: RUN-009 makes .editorconfig the authoritative convention source and the oracle explicitly treats low-level style values as outside policy scope (EXC-003); severities are suggestion/silent, so no build outcome is restricted. | IDE/dotnet format suggestions follow these values.
O CLAUDE.md 11-11 ER X47 - | **Default** — deviation needs a concrete reason and must be reported | Registered as EXTRA: the vocabulary definition makes every Default rule carry a reporting duty on deviation. | Deviation from any Default must appear in the report with its reason.
